---
// The full-bleed red band near the bottom of every page. Identical on all
// pages by design — one large statement, no button and no per-page props, so
// it reads as a standing brand mark rather than a call to action.
//
// A <p> rather than a heading: the same words repeat on every page, so they
// carry no document structure and shouldn't sit in the heading outline.
---

<section class="red-band cta">
  <p class="cta__statement">Presence | Style | Elegance</p>
</section>

<style>
  .cta {
    padding: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 52px) var(--section-pad-x);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .cta__statement {
    margin: 0;
    /* Script face, so no --font-heading token: it is used only here. Ships
       with Windows and Office; the generic cursive keeps the tone elsewhere. */
    font-family: 'Brush Script MT', 'Brush Script Std', 'Segoe Script', cursive;
    /* The face has one weight — asking for 900 only gets a smeared synthetic
       bold, and tight tracking collides the joined strokes. */
    font-weight: 400;
    /* Kept on one line — it is a single short phrase, so a wrap would read as
       a mistake. The ceiling stops it outgrowing very wide monitors. The
       script face runs narrower than the old sans, so it sits centred with
       air either side rather than spanning the band. */
    font-size: min(6.2vw, 108px);
    /* Room for the descenders and the tall f/l loops, which 1.06 clipped. */
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: normal;
    text-align: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
